== PROTH EXACT LAWS (GF-derived, verify numerically) ==
  s=1: GF = t/((1-t)^2(1-2t^s)) + t/((1-t)(1-t^s)); matches data: True; dominant root 2^(1/1) = 2.0000
  s=2: GF = t/((1-t)^2(1-2t^s)) + t/((1-t)(1-t^s)); matches data: True; dominant root 2^(1/2) = 1.4142
  s=3: GF = t/((1-t)^2(1-2t^s)) + t/((1-t)(1-t^s)); matches data: True; dominant root 2^(1/3) = 1.2599
  => THE PROTH SHEAR SPECTRUM = 2^(1/s): 2, sqrt2 (the hypotenuse/pseudo-doubling constant at the owner's Fibonacci-analogous s=2), 2^(1/3), ...
  Pascal ladder roots x^s = x^(s-1)+1: 2, phi = 1.6180, 1.4656 (Narayana), ... => Pascal DOMINATES Proth at every shear s >= 2

