== the relational reading ==
  T_n = C(n,2) = |E(K_n)| = the RELATIONAL size of n (the owner's frame; = tournament arc count, the tiling-hypercube dimension m = C(n-1,2) + base path)
  DICHOTOMY (measured above): relational families (simplex: counting sub-relations) shear EXPONENTIALLY (phi-ladder);
  positional families (polygonal/centered/pronic: dot patterns) shear POLYNOMIALLY; Faulhaber and pyramidal (sum-of-positional) polynomial one degree up;
  the Proth grid (doubling x relation-edge) shears exponentially on the 2^(1/s) ladder BELOW the relational phi-ladder.

DONE.

